# Line endings for YAML, and only YAML.
#
# `ai/knowledge/page/*.yaml` is parsed line by line by ai/knowledge/yaml.ts. That
# parser is now CRLF-tolerant, so this file is not what keeps the generator
# running - it is what stops the bytes from diverging by platform in the first
# place. Without it, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows installer default)
# checks a file committed as LF out as CRLF, and every one of these files reads as
# fully rewritten to any tool that compares bytes rather than lines.
#
# Deliberately narrow. A blanket `* text=auto` would invite Git to sniff and
# rewrite the .xlsx workbooks, .png evidence, .docx/.pptx documents, .pem keys and
# .dat report blobs this repository also tracks. Line endings are only ever a
# question for files something reads as lines; nothing here needs that but YAML.
#
# Existing working copies keep whatever they were checked out with - Git converts
# on checkout, not on demand. `git add --renormalize .` refreshes them if you want
# the on-disk bytes to match; with the parser fix in place it is cosmetic.
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
